| Read a file, image, or PDF | `Read` | `cat`, `head`, `tail`, `sed -n` |
| Change part of an existing file | `Edit` | `sed -i`, `awk`, `perl -i` |
| Create or fully rewrite a file | `Write` | heredocs, `echo >`, `tee` |
| Edit a Jupyter notebook cell | `NotebookEdit` | editing the `.ipynb` JSON |
| Read a web page | `WebFetch` | `curl`, `wget` |
| Search the web | `WebSearch` | `curl` against a search engine |
| Ask the user to choose | `AskUserQuestion` | an open question at the end of a turn |
| Delegate parallel or broad work | `Agent` | nested `claude -p` invocations |
| Run builds, tests, `git`, and searches | `Bash` | — |

- Search the tree with `Grep` and `Glob` when this session offers them; otherwise use `grep` and `find` through `Bash`.
- Start long-running commands with `Bash`'s `run_in_background` option, not a trailing `&`, and do not poll them with `sleep`.
- Read a file with `Read` before changing it with `Edit` or `Write`.
